<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolphe, Grand Duke of Luxembourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1905</span> · Also known as Adolphe of Nassau, Adolphe, Duke of Nassau, Adolphe of Nassau-Weilburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolphe was the last Duke of Nassau, from 1839 to 1866, and Grand Duke of Luxembourg from 1890 to 1905. He lost his duchy when he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> annexed it in 1866. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-the-netherlands">William III of the Netherlands</a> died without a male heir in 1890, Adolphe inherited Luxembourg under the Nassau family pact, ending its personal union with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolphe-grand-duke-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="Adolphe, Grand Duke of Luxembourg" width="269" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolfluxembourg1817-6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
